.TH CREATE\-ADDRESS 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.2.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
create\-address \- contract address from CREATE (deployer, nonce) or CREATE2 (EIP\-1014: deployer, salt, init code), offline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
create\-address [\-\-deployer ADDR (\-\-nonce N | \-\-salt HEX32 (\-\-init\-code\-hash HEX32 | \-\-init\-code HEX))]
With no flags, reads JSON from stdin: a tx / eth_getTransactionByHash response (from, nonce) or {deployer, ...}.
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a deployment tx (eth_getTransactionByHash response, `from` + `nonce`) from stdin when no flags are given.
.nf
.RS 2
  create\-address \-\-deployer 0x6ac7ea33f8831ea9dcc53393aaa88b25a785dbf0 \-\-nonce 1
  create\-address \-\-deployer 0x1F98431c8aD98523631AE4a59f267346ea31F984 \-\-salt 0x.. \-\-init\-code\-hash 0x..
  create\-address < deploy\-tx.json
.RE
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
  \-\-deployer ADDR        deploying account or factory (EIP\-55 checked when mixed case)
  \-\-nonce N              CREATE: deployer nonce, decimal or 0x\-hex
  \-\-salt HEX32           CREATE2: 32\-byte salt
  \-\-init\-code\-hash HEX32 CREATE2: keccak256 of the init code
  \-\-init\-code HEX        CREATE2: the init code itself (hashed here)
.fi
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
Reads a deployment tx (eth_getTransactionByHash response, `from` + `nonce`) from stdin when no flags are given.
.nf
.RS 2
  create\-address < deploy\-tx.json
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
0
last status ok
.TP
2
last status bad_input
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ create\-address \-\-deployer 0x6ac7ea33f8831ea9dcc53393aaa88b25a785dbf0 \-\-nonce 1
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ create\-address \-\-deployer 0x6ac7ea33f8831ea9dcc53393aaa88b25a785dbf0
# exit 2, last status: bad_input
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It may open hostile wallet files and handle secrets: run it sealed and offline (./blocktools run; sealed\-run allows it).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
